1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:00,829
Part five.

2
00:00:00,829 --> 00:00:03,136
The one that saves the most time —

3
00:00:03,136 --> 00:00:06,327
filling in the employer's own application form.

4
00:00:06,627 --> 00:00:09,195
This is where applications quietly die.

5
00:00:09,195 --> 00:00:11,896
You have the résumé, you have the letter,

6
00:00:11,896 --> 00:00:21,051
and now there is a thirty field form on a portal you have never seen before, asking you for everything you have already written down twice.

7
00:00:21,051 --> 00:00:25,069
Auto Fill reads that form and completes it from your profile.

8
00:00:25,069 --> 00:00:26,650
On their site, not ours.

9
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:29,392
From the job, tap Apply on Portal.

10
00:00:29,692 --> 00:00:33,346
The employer's real application page opens inside the app,

11
00:00:33,346 --> 00:00:35,551
and the robot button comes with it.

12
00:00:35,851 --> 00:00:38,227
Tap the robot, then Auto Fill.

13
00:00:38,527 --> 00:00:42,279
It scans the form and matches each question to your profile.

14
00:00:42,579 --> 00:00:46,316
The questions that need a human are flagged, not guessed at.

15
00:00:46,616 --> 00:00:48,960
Then your files attach themselves.

16
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,873
And notice it attaches the right regional version of each one.

17
00:00:53,173 --> 00:00:55,403
You look it over, and you submit it.

18
00:00:55,703 --> 00:00:58,237
And it is logged on your dashboard as applied.

19
00:00:58,537 --> 00:01:00,555
And that is the whole loop.

20
00:01:00,555 --> 00:01:06,160
Set it up once, then find a job and apply, without typing it all out again.

21
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:09,673
CVApplyr. Free to start, on iPhone and Android.

